<%#
  Save our number before we ring.

  The panel has told caregivers to do this since the feature shipped, in a grey
  line under the number field, and never said which number -- the value lived in
  credentials and was printed nowhere. Our first caregiver's two consent calls
  were answered and dropped inside four seconds with no key pressed, which is
  what a screening handset does to an unknown number, and she reported that
  Remindly had never called her at all.

  So this is not a hint. It is the first step, it carries the digits, and it
  carries a message the caregiver can send on -- because the person who has to
  save the number is usually not the person reading this screen, and "ask them
  to add a contact" is exactly the kind of instruction that gets relayed as
  "something about a phone call".
%>
<% number = TelnyxVoiceService.caller_id_number %>
<% if number.present? %>
  <div class="rounded-md border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50 p-4">
    <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">
      First, get our number saved in <%= senior.display_name %>'s phone as <strong>Remindly</strong>.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-wide text-gray-900">
      <%= formatted_phone_number(number) %>
    </p>

    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">
      A saved number shows our name instead of an unknown caller, and phones set
      to silence unknown callers will ring for it rather than sending us to
      voicemail. This matters most for the very first call, the one that asks
      <%= senior.display_name %> to agree — a voicemail cannot press 1.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-3">
      <%= link_to "Download contact card",
            caller_id_card_path,
            class: "inline-flex items-center px-4 py-2 border border-gray-300 text-sm font-medium rounded-md text-gray-700 bg-white hover:bg-gray-50" %>
      <span class="ml-2 text-xs text-gray-600">
        A file you can send to <%= senior.display_name %>. Opening it saves the contact.
      </span>
    </p>

    <%#
      A message written for them to send, not a summary of one.

      Plain text in a field they can select, the same device the reminder-link
      panel uses for the address it hands out: this layout loads Tailwind from a
      CDN and no JavaScript of our own, and a copy button that silently does
      nothing is worse than a field somebody can select. Tapping selects the lot.
    %>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <label for="caller_id_message" class="block text-xs font-medium text-gray-700">
        Something to send <%= senior.display_name %> — tap to select, then copy
      </label>
      <textarea id="caller_id_message" readonly rows="4" onclick="this.select()"
                class="mt-1 w-full text-sm border border-gray-300 rounded-md bg-white p-2 font-mono"><%=
        "Hi #{senior.display_name}, I've set up Remindly to ring you with reminders. " \
        "Please save this number in your contacts as Remindly: #{formatted_phone_number(number)}. " \
        "It will call you once to check you're happy with that — answer and press 1. " \
        "Press 9 at any time and the calls stop. #{current_user.friendly_name}"
      %></textarea>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
